  "body": "Stacked on #2162 (merge #2162 first)\n\n## What changed\n- Added the clean-room Mach4 milling postprocessor in `assets/posts/mach4.cps`.\n- Left 3-axis programs in `G94` mode with `G20`/`G21` unit blocks, `G90 G94 G91.1 G40 G49 G17 G64` safety header, `G17`/`G18`/`G19` arcs, `G41`/`G42`/`G40` cutter compensation, `G54`..`G59` and `G54.1 P1`..`P248` work offsets, `G28`/`G53`/`G30` safe retracts, `G73`/`G81`/`G82`/`G83`/`G84`/`G85`/`G86`/`G89` canned cycles with decimal-second `P` dwells, and `G31` Macro B probing.\n- Added 3+2 indexed AC trunnion support in `G94` (no `G43.4` or `G93`) using `#1962`'s trunnion schema (`A` parent of `C`, `pivot`, `offset`, `zeroOffset`, `rollover`, `signConvention`, `controller.rtcp = false`).\n- Added analytical AC inverse kinematics, platter-center G54 datum transform (`work_datum = a_pivot + c_offset`), rotated cardinal arc projection, optional paired `rotaryUnclamp`/`rotaryClamp` M-codes, and safe-retract-only `C` rollover handling (`rollover_360` vs `unwrapped`).\n- Added named refusals when `controller.rtcp` is `true`, when AC trunnion geometry or travel bounds are invalid or missing, or when an indexed section changes tool orientation during cutting (`\"needs #1966: inverse-time feed\"`).\n- Registered `\"Mach4\"` in `BUILTINS` in `crates/app/src/posting.rs` and added `\"Mach4\"` conformance and script entries in `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs` and `crates/post/tests/script_mach4.rs`.\n- Documented unattended choices in `docs/decisions/1968-mach4-post.md`.\n\n## Cause\nCamcraft shipped no Mach4 milling dialect, and Mach4 controllers lack native Fanuc `G43.4` RTCP while `#1966` (`G93` inverse-time feed) is not yet merged.\n\n## Tests\n- Pins added (all failed red before implementation):\n  - `crates/post/tests/mach4_post.rs` (3 tests: 3-axis mm/inch dialect words and cycles, `G31` probing, `G53`/`G30` safe retracts)\n  - `crates/post/tests/mach4_trunnion.rs` (3 tests: mm/inch `table_rh`/`tool_rh` 3+2 kinematics verified via `forward_part`, rollover `[0, 360)` and clamp M-code ordering, RTCP/trunnion-geometry/simultaneous refusals)\n  - `crates/app/tests/mach4_builtin.rs` (2 tests: `BUILTINS` + `post_serves`, end-to-end `post_setup` on `3axis-vmc.mch`)\n  - `crates/post/tests/script_mach4.rs` (`post_suite!(\"mach4.cps\")`, 11 recorded cases)\n- Mutation checks verified (each turned pinning tests red, then returned green on restore):\n  - Removed `\"Mach4\"` from `BUILTINS` in `crates/app/src/posting.rs`: `mach4_builtin` failed (`0 passed; 2 failed`).\n  - Bypassed `m.rtcp === true` check in `assets/posts/mach4.cps`: `mach4_refuses_rtcp_bad_trunnion_and_simultaneous_by_name` failed.\n  - Bypassed simultaneous mid-section orientation guard in `assets/posts/mach4.cps`: `mach4_refuses_rtcp_bad_trunnion_and_simultaneous_by_name` failed.\n  - Bypassed `cRollover` wrapping in `assets/posts/mach4.cps`: `mach4_rotary_rollover_unwrapped_vs_360_and_clamp_order` failed.\n  - Bypassed missing `A.pivot` guard in `assets/posts/mach4.cps`: `mach4_refuses_rtcp_bad_trunnion_and_simultaneous_by_name` failed.\n- Checks run after final edit:\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green (0 warnings).\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (`post` 17s, `motion` 1166s, `app` 2067s, `ui` 303s; 4 steps, 0 failed).\n\n## Goldens moved\n- Zero existing `.nc` or `.cl` goldens changed (`git diff --stat base-2162 -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty).\n- Added 14 new Mach4 conformance goldens: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_mach4.nc` and 13 `.nc` files under `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/mach4/`.\n- Added 11 new `mach4.cps` recorded script verdicts under `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/mach4/` (7 `.nc`, 4 `.refusal`).\n\n## Not exercised\n- No physical Mach4 controller hardware run or Mach4 simulator GUI verification ran in CI; Mach4 syntax and RS-274 rules rest on public documentation and `camcraft_post::kinematics::forward_part` round-trips.\n- Simultaneous 4/5-axis `G93` inverse-time cutting waits for `#1966` and refuses by name until then.\n\n## Overlaps\n- Stacked on `#2162` (`issue/1962-trunnion-schema`) for `#1962` AC trunnion fields and kinematics (`base-2162`).\n- Open PRs `#2293`, `#2290`, `#2253`, `#2149`, and `#2136` touch other parts of `crates/app/src/posting.rs` and not `BUILTINS` (`posting.rs` `BUILTINS` touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes).\n\nChangelog: Add clean-room Mach4 milling postprocessor with 3-axis G94 and 3+2 AC trunnion support.\nFixes #1968\n",
